IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `tfa-dates`
IMPORT `tfa-rules`
IMPORT `tfa-seat`

-- Fatal Accidents Act 1934 (Tas) -- worked cases for the family member's questions (tfa-seat.l4), the date helper
-- (tfa-dates.l4) and the rules (tfa-rules.l4). Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was
-- copied from the encoding's output. Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The
-- facts are illustrative.
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on material from the Tasmanian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (c) State of Tasmania, CC BY
-- 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`
`any day` MEANS `d` 1 1 2000

§§ `s 3 -- am I a member of the family`

#ASSERT `Am I a member of the family of the person who died` `spouse` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A spouse needs no relationship at the time of the wrongful act (finding 1): married after the act, still family.
#ASSERT `Am I a member of the family of the person who died` `spouse` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a member of the family of the person who died` `partner in a personal relationship` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A partner whose relationship began after the wrongful act is not a "partner" (s 3: "at the time when").
#ASSERT `Am I a member of the family of the person who died` `partner in a personal relationship` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Am I a member of the family of the person who died` `parent` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a member of the family of the person who died` `stepparent` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a member of the family of the person who died` `grandparent` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a member of the family of the person who died` `child` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a member of the family of the person who died` `stepchild` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a member of the family of the person who died` `grandchild` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a member of the family of the person who died` `brother` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a member of the family of the person who died` `sister` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a member of the family of the person who died` `half-brother` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Am I a member of the family of the person who died` `half-sister` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An aunt, niece, cousin or in-law: the "means" list is closed (finding 2).
#ASSERT `Am I a member of the family of the person who died` `another relationship` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 3-6 -- can an action be brought for my benefit`

#ASSERT `Can an action be brought for my benefit for this death` `child` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can an action be brought for my benefit for this death` `partner in a personal relationship` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 6: only one action lies.
#ASSERT `Can an action be brought for my benefit for this death` `child` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 4: no wrongful act, neglect or default; or the deceased could not have sued.
#ASSERT `Can an action be brought for my benefit for this death` `child` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can an action be brought for my benefit for this death` `child` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 3/s 5: not a member of the family.
#ASSERT `Can an action be brought for my benefit for this death` `another relationship` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can an action be brought for my benefit for this death` `partner in a personal relationship` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 8(1) -- from when can I bring it in my own name`

#ASSERT `the corresponding day` 6 `months after` (`d` 31 3 2025) EQUALS `d` 30 9 2025
#ASSERT `the corresponding day` 6 `months after` (`d` 15 7 2025) EQUALS `d` 15 1 2026
#ASSERT `the corresponding day` 6 `months after` (`d` 31 8 2023) EQUALS `d` 29 2 2024

#ASSERT `From when can I bring the action in my own name` `sister` FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 10 1 2025) EQUALS `you may bring it now, as there is no executor or administrator`
-- Death 10 January 2025: the 6 months end on 10 July 2025; from 11 July 2025.
#ASSERT `From when can I bring the action in my own name` `sister` FALSE TRUE FALSE (`d` 10 1 2025) EQUALS `you may bring it from` (`d` 11 7 2025)
-- Death 31 August 2025: the 6 months end on 28 February 2026; from 1 March 2026.
#ASSERT `From when can I bring the action in my own name` `child` FALSE TRUE FALSE (`d` 31 8 2025) EQUALS `you may bring it from` (`d` 1 3 2026)
-- Death 31 August 2023: the 6 months end on 29 February 2024; from 1 March 2024.
#ASSERT `From when can I bring the action in my own name` `child` FALSE TRUE FALSE (`d` 31 8 2023) EQUALS `you may bring it from` (`d` 1 3 2024)
-- Death 30 September 2025: the 6 months end on 30 March 2026; from 31 March 2026.
#ASSERT `From when can I bring the action in my own name` `parent` FALSE TRUE FALSE (`d` 30 9 2025) EQUALS `you may bring it from` (`d` 31 3 2026)
-- Death 15 July 2025: across the year end, from 16 January 2026.
#ASSERT `From when can I bring the action in my own name` `parent` FALSE TRUE FALSE (`d` 15 7 2025) EQUALS `you may bring it from` (`d` 16 1 2026)
#ASSERT `From when can I bring the action in my own name` `parent` FALSE TRUE TRUE (`d` 15 7 2025) EQUALS `no, an action for this death has already been brought`
#ASSERT `From when can I bring the action in my own name` `another relationship` FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 15 7 2025) EQUALS `no, you are not a member of the family for whose benefit it is brought`

§§ `ss 5, 6, 8(1) -- can I bring it in my own name on this day`

-- Death 10 January 2025, an executor who has not sued: not on the last day of the 6 months, yes the day after.
#ASSERT `Can I bring the action in my own name on this day` `spouse` FALSE TRUE FALSE (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 10 7 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I bring the action in my own name on this day` `spouse` FALSE TRUE FALSE (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 11 7 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I bring the action in my own name on this day` `spouse` FALSE TRUE FALSE (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 1 2 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I bring the action in my own name on this day` `spouse` FALSE TRUE FALSE (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 10 1 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I bring the action in my own name on this day` `spouse` FALSE TRUE FALSE (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 1 6 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Death 31 August 2025: not on 28 February 2026, yes on 1 March 2026.
#ASSERT `Can I bring the action in my own name on this day` `grandchild` FALSE TRUE FALSE (`d` 31 8 2025) (`d` 28 2 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I bring the action in my own name on this day` `grandchild` FALSE TRUE FALSE (`d` 31 8 2025) (`d` 1 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- No executor or administrator: at once.
#ASSERT `Can I bring the action in my own name on this day` `spouse` FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 1 2 2025) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- An action already brought (s 6), even after the 6 months.
#ASSERT `Can I bring the action in my own name on this day` `spouse` FALSE TRUE TRUE (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 1 6 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I bring the action in my own name on this day` `spouse` FALSE FALSE TRUE (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 1 2 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not a member of the family.
#ASSERT `Can I bring the action in my own name on this day` `another relationship` FALSE FALSE FALSE (`d` 10 1 2025) (`d` 1 2 2025) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 7 -- particulars`

-- No statement of claim delivered yet: the duty has not arisen.
#ASSERT `Have I delivered the particulars section 7 requires` FALSE `any day` FALSE `any day` `the defendant` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The same day, to the defendant or the defendant's lawyer, covering both: yes.
#ASSERT `Have I delivered the particulars section 7 requires` TRUE (`d` 3 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 3 3 2025) `the defendant` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Have I delivered the particulars section 7 requires` TRUE (`d` 3 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 3 3 2025) `the defendant's Australian legal practitioner` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The next day, or the day before: not "together with" the statement of claim.
#ASSERT `Have I delivered the particulars section 7 requires` TRUE (`d` 3 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 4 3 2025) `the defendant` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Have I delivered the particulars section 7 requires` TRUE (`d` 3 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 2 3 2025) `the defendant` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- To someone else; missing the persons; missing the nature of the claim; none delivered.
#ASSERT `Have I delivered the particulars section 7 requires` TRUE (`d` 3 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 3 3 2025) `someone else` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Have I delivered the particulars section 7 requires` TRUE (`d` 3 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 3 3 2025) `the defendant` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Have I delivered the particulars section 7 requires` TRUE (`d` 3 3 2025) TRUE (`d` 3 3 2025) `the defendant` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Have I delivered the particulars section 7 requires` TRUE (`d` 3 3 2025) FALSE (`d` 3 3 2025) `the defendant` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 10(1) -- what is not taken off the damages`

#ASSERT `Can this payment be taken off our damages` `a sum under a contract of insurance or assurance paid or payable on the death` 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can this payment be taken off our damages` `a sum from a superannuation, provident or like fund` 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can this payment be taken off our damages` `a benefit from a friendly society, benefit society or trade union` 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can this payment be taken off our damages` `a pension, benefit or allowance under the Veterans' Entitlements Act 1986` 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can this payment be taken off our damages` `a pension, benefit or allowance under the Social Security Act 1991` 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The estate: at $250 000 not at all; a dollar above, that dollar.
#ASSERT `Can this payment be taken off our damages` `the part of the estate that passes to members of the family` 250000 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can this payment be taken off our damages` `the part of the estate that passes to members of the family` 250001 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can this payment be taken off our damages` `the part of the estate that passes to members of the family` 400000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can this payment be taken off our damages` `the part of the estate that passes to members of the family` 0 EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Anything else (for example workers compensation): the Act is silent.
#ASSERT `Can this payment be taken off our damages` `another payment or benefit` 0 EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `How much of the estate can be counted against our damages` 250000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How much of the estate can be counted against our damages` 250001 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `How much of the estate can be counted against our damages` 400000 EQUALS 150000
#ASSERT `How much of the estate can be counted against our damages` 100000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How much of the estate can be counted against our damages` 0 EQUALS 0

§§ `s 10(2) -- funeral, headstone, hospital and medical expenses`

#ASSERT `How much can our damages include for this expense` `funeral or cremation expenses` 9500 TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 9500
-- Paid by someone outside the action (for example an employer): nothing under s 10(2).
#ASSERT `How much can our damages include for this expense` `funeral or cremation expenses` 9500 FALSE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 0
-- Headstone: the lower of the amount paid and the reasonable cost.
#ASSERT `How much can our damages include for this expense` `the cost of erecting a headstone or tombstone over the grave` 8000 TRUE FALSE 6000 EQUALS JUST 6000
#ASSERT `How much can our damages include for this expense` `the cost of erecting a headstone or tombstone over the grave` 5000 TRUE FALSE 6000 EQUALS JUST 5000
#ASSERT `How much can our damages include for this expense` `the cost of erecting a headstone or tombstone over the grave` 6000 TRUE FALSE 6000 EQUALS JUST 6000
#ASSERT `How much can our damages include for this expense` `the cost of erecting a headstone or tombstone over the grave` 6000 FALSE FALSE 6000 EQUALS JUST 0
-- Hospital and medical: only if incurred as a result of the wrongful act.
#ASSERT `How much can our damages include for this expense` `hospital and medical expenses` 12000 TRUE TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST 12000
#ASSERT `How much can our damages include for this expense` `hospital and medical expenses` 12000 TRUE FALSE 0 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `How much can our damages include for this expense` `hospital and medical expenses` 12000 FALSE TRUE 0 EQUALS JUST 0
-- Another expense (for example a wake): s 10(2) is silent.
#ASSERT `How much can our damages include for this expense` `another expense` 3000 TRUE TRUE 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 5 -- dividing the amount recovered`

-- $300 000 recovered, $20 000 costs not recovered, my share half: $140 000.
#ASSERT `How much of the amount recovered do I receive` 300000 20000 150000 300000 EQUALS 140000
#ASSERT `How much of the amount recovered do I receive` 100000 0 25000 100000 EQUALS 25000
-- A third of $90 000 ($120 000 less $30 000).
#ASSERT `How much of the amount recovered do I receive` 120000 30000 40000 120000 EQUALS 30000
-- Costs above the amount recovered: nothing to divide.
#ASSERT `How much of the amount recovered do I receive` 10000 15000 5000 10000 EQUALS 0
-- No shares directed.
#ASSERT `How much of the amount recovered do I receive` 10000 0 0 0 EQUALS 0

§§ `s 9 -- money paid into court`

#ASSERT `Does the defendant win the issue on the money paid into court` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does the defendant win the issue on the money paid into court` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the defendant win the issue on the money paid into court` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the defendant win the issue on the money paid into court` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the defendant win the issue on the money paid into court` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
